' Question: what happens, in order, when the owner presses Run on the Backtest workbench?
' Explained by: ../06-runtime.md. Drawn by hand, high level.
@startuml 06-backtest-run
participant "BacktestWorkbench\n(UI thread)" as W
participant BacktestRunCoordinator as C
participant "pool worker" as P
participant RunBacktestQueryHandler as Q
participant "the kind's\nIKindBacktester" as B
participant "market_data\n(stored candles)" as M

W -> W : the fence opens an action (id n)\nactivity IDLE --> RUNNING
W -> C : start_backtest(n, RunBacktestQuery(kind, request))
C -> P : the query with a cancel flag
P -> Q : execute(query)
Q -> B : run(request) for the kind the catalog names
B -> M : read stored candles, 1-second klines, funding
alt the period is stored
  B --> W : BacktestOutcome (candles, equity, fills, figures, notes)
  W -> W : n is still current: show the result\nactivity RUNNING --> IDLE
else candles missing
  B --> W : BacktestRefusal(missing candles)
  W -> W : offer "Sync candles"; only a click syncs
else Cancel pressed, or another bot selected
  W -> W : the fence drops n at once; the flag stops the worker
  note over W : a late answer for n is dropped and logged;\nthe last result stays on screen after a Cancel
end
@enduml
